## Changes

### 1. PPO returns & advantages — [`mind/continual_learner.py`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/mind/continual_learner.py)
- **Stopped normalising the returns.** `_do_ppo_update` used
  `returns = (returns - mean) / std` per batch, then `advantage = return - value`
  and `critic_loss = smooth_l1(value, returns)`. Normalising the returns makes
  the critic's target non-stationary — it rescales every update — so the value
  head never converges and the advantage signal is noise. This is the single
  biggest reason training never improved.
- **Now:** returns are the raw discounted reward-to-go, computed with
  **episode-boundary resets** (`running = 0` at every `done`) and an
  **edge bootstrap** (`running = last.value` if the buffer doesn't end on a
  terminal step). Only the *advantage* is normalised, and only for the
  policy-gradient term. The critic regresses to the raw returns.
- **On-policy rollouts.** The 256-slot buffer was re-trained every 64 ticks →
  each transition used ~4× with a stale `old_log_prob`. Buffer is now cleared
  after every update and `CONTINUAL_UPDATE_EVERY == CONTINUAL_BUFFER_SIZE`, so
  every transition trains exactly once (× `CONTINUAL_MINI_EPOCHS`).
- Added `Transition.done` and `ContinualLearner.flush()` (force an update at an
  episode boundary).
- `_maybe_grow()` gated behind `config_rl.MIND_GROWTH_ENABLED` (default `False`).
- `[PPO]` log line prints once per update instead of once per mini-epoch.

### 2. Config — [`config_rl.py`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/config_rl.py)
- `LEARNING_RATE` `1e-4 → 3e-4` (PPO default; 1e-4 barely moved a from-scratch policy).
- `ENTROPY_COEFF` `0.01 → 0.005` (0.01 was strong enough to fight convergence on small action spaces).
- `CONTINUAL_UPDATE_EVERY` `64 → 256` (== buffer size; see above).
- Added `MIND_GROWTH_ENABLED = False`.

### 3. Run loop — [`main.py`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/main.py)
- Both `learner.collect(...)` calls now pass `done=done`.
- Episode-boundary `learner.maybe_update()` → `learner.flush()` in `run_gui` and `run_headless`.

### 4. Reward scale — [`rewards.py`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/rewards.py)
- `R_OCEAN_DEATH` `-500.0 → -15.0`. `ats_env` applies it on every shark trigger
  (including survived strikes); a single -500 tick dominates the whole return and,
  after advantage normalisation, flattens every other transition in the rollout.

### 5. Object embedding bug — [`model_rl.py`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/model_rl.py)
- `forward()` did `state[..., 19].long()`, but index 19 is the nearest-object id
  **normalised** as `id / ITEM_VOCAB_SIZE`. `.long()` on a 0..1 fraction is
  always 0, so the 100×32 item-embedding table was only ever read at row 0.
  Now de-normalised (`* ITEM_VOCAB_SIZE`, rounded). Entity index 15 is a raw int
  and was already fine.
- No parameter-shape change; old checkpoints still load.

### 6. train_rl.py — [`train_rl.py`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/train_rl.py)
- Same return-normalisation fix as (1).
- `RewardEngine` was used at line ~101 without an import → `NameError` on the
  first episode. Added the import. (`main.py --train` was dead.)

### 7. Sanity harness — NEW
- [`sanity_env.py`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/sanity_env.py) — a
  7×7 navigate-to-goal grid with the same `STATE_SIZE` / `ACTION_SIZE` and the
  same `reset()/step()/action_mask()` interface as `ATSEnvironment`. **Not part
  of the world.**
- [`sanity_train.py`](file:///c:/Users/Bob/Documents/github/ATS/sanity_train.py) —
  trains a fresh `RLPolicy` through the real `ContinualLearner` and asserts
  reward + goal-reach rate climb above the learner's own early episodes and a
  random policy. ~40s, deterministic. Run it before any long ATS training run.

